WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.366
You can now quickly assess device fleet security on the Knox Admin Portal. With the security dashboard, you can see which devices

00:00:08.366 --> 00:00:15.699
are approaching end-of-life and need to be replaced, which devices are missing critical security updates, and what are the latest OS

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.266
and security patch versions available for each device in your fleet.

00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:27.633
You can reach the Knox Admin Portal's Security dashboard by clicking its tile on the homepage.

00:00:27.633 --> 00:00:28.366


00:00:28.366 --> 00:00:35.932
The "Device lifecycle summary" section shows a quick overview of your fleet's security status. Letting you know how many devices need

00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:44.766
security updates, are past their security patch end-of-life dates, or had their security patch cadence changed in the last 3 months. This

00:00:44.766 --> 00:00:53.066
section only shows devices with at least one of the issues mentioned above that are enrolled in Knox Mobile Enrollment, Knox E-FOTA, or Knox

00:00:53.066 --> 00:00:54.666
Asset Intelligence.

00:00:54.666 --> 00:00:56.632


00:00:56.633 --> 00:01:05.633
You can click the tiles to see which devices are impacted for each metric. For example, the "Devices not-up-to-date" metric tells you which

00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:08.566
devices are lagging behind on their security patches.

00:01:08.566 --> 00:01:10.966


00:01:10.966 --> 00:01:17.899
The "Device lifecycle information" section lists all devices in your account (Except for devices enrolled exclusively to Knox Manage or Knox

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:23.633
Guard), and shows their security and OS information, grouped by device models and buyer codes.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:32.633
The "Knox E-FOTA" section provides OS and security patch data for devices enrolled to Knox E-FOTA

00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:35.899
giving visibility into firmware update compliance.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:40.700
This provides insight into firmware distribution and patch adoption across your fleet.

00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:48.133
The "Knox Asset Intelligence" section lets you see how many vulnerabilities were detected on devices enrolled to "Knox Asset Intelligence",

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:52.699
and shows which devices have passed or failed integrity checks.

00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:58.399
You can click the arrow to see the Knox Asset Intelligence Security Center.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:01:58.666


00:01:58.666 --> 00:02:07.032
Which gives comprehensive vulnerability and integrity dashboards, fleet-wide charts, and lets you download reports for deeper analysis.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:13.766
To learn more about Knox Security Dashboard, see our documentation at docs.samsungknox.com. Thanks for watching!
